From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek-v4-flash: FP8 wo_a and chunked KV compressor (memory)

VLLM_DSV4_WOA_FP8=1 (default 0): sm_80 wo_a runs from the FP8 checkpoint
weight (Triton thin GEMM, e4m3 decoded four bytes at a time) instead of a
bf16 copy built at first use (64 MiB/layer, ~1 GiB per PP rank). Above 128
tokens the weight is dequantized per call into a transient buffer and the
unchanged einsum runs (bitwise equal to the bf16 path).

VLLM_DSV4_COMPRESS_CHUNKED=1 (default 0): the ratio-128 KV compressor kernel
loaded a [256, 512] fp32 tile twice and spilled 10-22 KB per thread; the
driver reserves that local memory for the device's full thread capacity
(~1.3 GiB per GPU outside the caching allocator). Online max / sum / weighted
sum over 8-row slices: no stack, faster; reduction order differs from
tl.softmax (1 of 9321 cache bytes differed in a synthetic test).

PP3 on CMP 170HX, KV 2.5 GiB: device use 61.8/64.5/63.9 -> 58.8/61.4/60.8 GB.
Both are in the dsv4-flash profile.

---
